## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical Android data layer skills: Room, Retrofit, coroutines, Flow, and offline-first UX. Focus is on implementing a simple, robust data path with graceful fallback and deterministic refresh behavior.

## Key Concepts
- Room data access objects and migrations
- Retrofit API interfaces and JSON mapping
- Repository pattern with Flow/StateFlow
- Offline-first data synchronization and error handling
- ViewModel integration and simple UI trigger

## Code Example
```kotlin
// Data model
@Entity(tableName = "notes")
data class Note(
  @PrimaryKey val id: String,
  val title: String,
  val content: String,
  val updatedAt: Long
)

// DAO sketch
@Dao
interface NoteDao {
  @Query("SELECT * FROM notes ORDER BY updatedAt DESC")
  fun observeNotes(): Flow<List<Note>>

  @Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)
  suspend fun upsert(notes: List<Note>)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test race conditions between local and remote updates?
- What backoff strategy would you use for network retries and why?

## Why This Question Is Asked
Tests the candidate's understanding of process isolation, security best practices, and production-grade feature rollouts in Android applications.

## Key Concepts
- Isolated Android process with Binder/AIDL IPC
- Server-signed configuration verification using hardware-backed Android Keystore
- Encrypted Room storage with per-user deterministic rollout logic
- Offline mode with audit trail and IPC rate limiting

## Code Example
```java
// AIDL IPC surface
public interface IFlagService extends IInterface {
    boolean isFlagEnabled(String userId, String flagKey) throws RemoteException;
    List<FeatureFlag> getAllFlags(String userId) throws RemoteException;
}

// Isolated process service
public class FlagEngineService extends Service {
    private final IFlagService.Stub mBinder = new IFlagService.Stub() {
        @Override
        public boolean isFlagEnabled(String userId, String flagKey) throws RemoteException {
            return flagEngine.isEnabled(userId, flagKey);
        }
    };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of core Android app architecture: data layer with Room, network layer with Retrofit, UI with Jetpack Compose, and a practical accessibility feature (TTS). It also touches lifecycle awareness and basic testing strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Room: entity, DAO, migrations (basic)
- Retrofit: service interfaces and data models
- Kotlin Flow: streaming data from repository to UI
- Jetpack Compose: LazyColumn rendering
- TextToSpeech: initialization, lifecycle handling, easing for UI
- Testing: unit tests for data layer; instrumentation for TTS and UI flows

## Code Example

```kotlin
// Entity
@Entity(tableName = "headlines")
data class Headline(
  @PrimaryKey val id: String,
  val title: String,
  val timestamp: Long
)

// DAO
@Dao
interface HeadlineDao {
  @Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)
  suspend fun insertAll(headlines: List<Headline>)

  @Query("SELECT * FROM headlines ORDER BY timestamp DESC")
  fun getAll(): Flow<List<Headline>>
}
```

```kotlin
// Retrofit service
interface HeadlinesService {
  @GET("headlines")
  suspend fun fetchHeadlines(): List<Headline>
}
```

```kotlin
// Repository sketch
class HeadlinesRepo(private val dao: HeadlineDao, private val svc: HeadlinesService) {
  val headlines: Flow<List<Headline>> = dao.getAll()

  suspend fun refresh() {
    val fresh = svc.fetchHeadlines()
    dao.insertAll(fresh)
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle offline-first behavior and cache invalidation?
- How would you test TTS integration and ensure accessibility support across locales?

## Why This Is Asked
This probes offline data handling, secure at-rest storage, and IPC via bound services—core Android concepts for robust, privacy-minded apps.

## Key Concepts
- Room with encryption (SQLCipher) and Keystore-wrapped key
- Event data model (id, timestamp, type, payload)
- DAO queries for last N records
- Bound service with Binder interface for internal components
- Lifecycle considerations and test strategy

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity(tableName = "events") data class Event(
  @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true) val id: Long = 0,
  val timestamp: Long,
  val type: String,
  val payload: String?
)
@Dao interface EventDao {
  @Query("SELECT * FROM events ORDER BY timestamp DESC LIMIT :limit") fun getLastEvents(limit: Int): List<Event>
  @Insert fun insert(event: Event)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle schema migrations for the encrypted database?
- How would you test border cases like rapid successive events or large payloads?

## Why This Is Asked
This checks practical ability to implement stable background work with WorkManager, persistent config storage via DataStore, and a simple UI-facing trigger.

## Key Concepts
- WorkManager periodic tasks with constraints
- CoroutineWorker pattern
- DataStore for small config persistence
- Flow/LiveData for UI updates
- Retry/backoff and error handling

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Serializable
data class Config(val version: String, val features: Map<String, Boolean>)

class ConfigWorker(appContext: Context, params: WorkerParameters) : CoroutineWorker(appContext, params) {
    override suspend fun doWork(): Result {
        val url = inputData.getString("url") ?: return Result.failure()
        // network fetch and parse omitted for brevity
        return Result.success()
    }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test failure scenarios (network error, invalid JSON)?
- How would you prevent duplicate work when the app restarts?

## Why This Is Asked

New angle introduces multi-cache offline view and scheduled refresh, probing data modeling, cache invalidation, and basic MVVM patterns.

## Key Concepts
- Room entities and relations
- Separate body cache design
- MVVM with Repository
- WorkManager with constraints
- Simple search SQL LIKE

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity(tableName = "article_meta")
data class ArticleMeta(
  @PrimaryKey val id: String,
  val title: String,
  val excerpt: String,
  val updatedAt: Long
)

@Entity(tableName = "article_body")
data class ArticleBody(
  @PrimaryKey val articleId: String,
  val body: String
)

@Dao
interface ArticleDao {
  @Query("SELECT * FROM article_meta WHERE title LIKE :query || '%'")
  fun searchByTitle(query: String): List<ArticleMeta>

  @Transaction
  @Query("SELECT * FROM article_meta WHERE id = :id")
  fun getArticleWithBody(id: String): ArticleWithBody
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle cache invalidation and staleness if the remote API updates articles?
- What tests would you write to verify offline viewing, search correctness, and refresh reliability?
